  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper studies quantum‑inspired ML for banking tasks. A DPP‑enhanced Random Forest improves churn‑prediction precision from 71.6% to 77.5% (classical experiment), while quantum hardware tests run small DPP circuits (≤8 qubits) on IBM Guadalupe. For credit‑risk prediction, orthogonal/compound quantum‑inspired neural layers achieve ~54% Gini with only 13 parameters vs 64 for a classical network, and hardware inference on IBM Hanoi yields 50.19% Gini (53.68% with mitigation) compared to 54.19% in noiseless simulation.",
